RESOLUTION NO. 16425
A RESOLUTION OF THE CITY COUNCIL OF THE CITY OF REDWOOD
CITY CALLING FOR AN ELECTION TO BE CONSOLIDATED WITH THE
GENERAL MUNICIPAL ELECTION AND STATEWIDE GENERAL
ELECTION ON NOVEMBER 3, 2026 AND SUBMITTING TO THE
VOTERS AT THAT ELECTION AN INITIATIVE MEASURE TO AMEND
THE REDWOOD CITY CODE TO IMPOSE ADDITIONAL RENT
CONTROL AND JUST CAUSE EVICTION LIMITS
WHEREAS, on October 29, 2025, three Redwood City residents (“the
Proponents”) submitted to the City’s Elections Official a Notice of Intent to Circulate an
Initiative Petition for an initative measure known as the Redwood City Fair and Affordable
Housing Ordinance; and
WHEREAS, on April 23, 2026, the Proponents presented petition signatures to the
City Clerk at which time the City Clerk determined there to be a sufficient number of
signatures, prima facie, to proceed with accepting the petition as filed and conducting a
full verification of the petition signatures; and
WHEREAS, on May 13, 2026, the San Mateo County Elections Office informed
the City Clerk that their review of the petition signatures confirmed the total number of
valid signatures on the petition was 4,751, which exceeded the required number of
signatures per California Elections Code Section 9215; and
WHEREAS, on May 19, 2026, the City Clerk issued a Certificate of Sufficiency to
the City Council setting forth facts establishing that the petition was signed by not less
than 10 percent of the voters of the City and therefore was sufficient; and
WHEREAS, on June 8, 2026 the City Council accepted certification of signature
verification for the initiative petition, received an initial report and requested a
supplemental report pursuant to California Elections Code Section 9212 which provides
additional information regarding the impacts of the proposed ordinance; and
WHEREAS, on June 22, 2026 the City Council adopted Resolution No. 16415
calling for the holding of a General Municipal Election on Tuesday, November 3, 2026 for
the election of three municipal officers; and
WHEREAS, on June 22, 2026, the City Council adopted Resolution No.16416
requesting the Board of Supervisors of the County of San Mateo to consolidate the
aforesaid General Municipal Election with the Statewide General Election; and
WHEREAS, pursuant to Elections Code Section 9215, the City Council has
decided to call an election to submit to the voters the Redwood City Fair and Affordable
Housing Ordinance and desires to place it on the ballot and consolidate that election with
the aforesaid consolidated election.
